      },
      {
        "src": "/portfolio/village-evening/02.webp",
        "thumbnail": "/portfolio/village-evening/02-preview.webp",
        "alt": "At 5 a.m — angled view",
        "label": "Angled view",
        "width": 1990,
        "height": 1505
      }
    ],
    "description": "Another superthick palette knife painting. For this one I mixed my oil paints with a homemade painting medium: dammar, stand oil and refined turpentine - the mix I turn to when I have to move or feel too tired/lazy to prepare an egg emulsion.\n\nI doubt I’ll ever see these places again. When I was a child, I loved visiting my uncle in the countryside near lake Ilmen cause I was absolutly free to explore the fields and woods near his house and come back whenever I liked. He didn’t mind.\n\nOil on canvas\n18*24 cm",
    "sources": [
      {
        "label": "DeviantArt",
        "url": "https://www.deviantart.com/alinaivy/art/At-5-a.m-1387821362"
      }
    ]
